      "script": "My apartment neighbor kept parking in my numbered space because it was closer to his door. I left a note. He threw it under my windshield wiper with ‘first come, first served’ written across it. The lease disagreed. Management warned him twice, then told me to call their towing company if it happened again. Friday night, his truck was back, perfectly centered over my painted number. I photographed the truck, the sign, and my lease, then made the call. He came outside while the driver was lifting it and insisted the space belonged to visitors. The driver checked the parking map. His own signed lease assigned him a different spot beside the dumpster. A modest scenic upgrade. He paid $286 to recover the truck and started using his actual space. On Monday, management billed him another $75 for removing the warning sticker. My space has been mysteriously available ever since.",
